claim.claim-text:
a first dielectric layer of the dielectric material having a first surface and a second opposing surface;
a first ground plane disposed on the first surface;
a metalized layer formed on the second opposing surface and including a first aperture;
one or more conductive structures extending at least partially between the first surface and the second opposing surface, the one or more conductive structures, the first ground plane and the metalized layer define a corresponding first resonant space within the first dielectric layer; and
a first radio frequency input-output (RF I/O) region located at the first surface and electrically isolated from the first ground plane by a first isolation region.

a second dielectric layer of the dielectric material having a third surface and a fourth opposing surface, the metalized layer positioned between the second opposing surface of the first dielectric layer and the third surface of the second dielectric layer;
a second ground plane disposed on the fourth opposing surface of the second dielectric layer; and
one or more second conductive structures extending at least partially between the third surface and the fourth opposing surface of the second dielectric layer, the one or more second conductive structures, the second ground plane and the metalized layer define a corresponding second resonant space within the second dielectric layer, the corresponding second resonant space adjacent, and electromagnetically coupled, to the corresponding first resonant space.

a third dielectric layer of the dielectric material having a fifth surface and a sixth opposing surface, the second ground layer positioned between the fourth opposing surface of the second dielectric layer and the fifth surface of the third dielectric layer, the second ground plane including a second aperture;
a third ground plane disposed on the sixth opposing surface of the third dielectric layer;
and
one or more third conductive structures extending at least partially between the fifth surface and the sixth opposing surface of the second dielectric layer, the one or more third conductive structures, the second ground plane and the third ground plane define a corresponding third resonant space within the third dielectric layer, the corresponding third resonant space adjacent, and electromagnetically coupled, to the corresponding second resonant space.
